unexpected argument: b.md
Usage of mdhtml:
mdhtml converts CommonMark to HTML.
  -blocks
    	print how many blocks the input reads as, the document's own included
  -gen sections
    	write the receipts' workload of this many sections and read nothing
  -highlight
    	mark Go's keywords in code blocks of language go
  -seed seed
    	the seed of the -gen workload (default 1)
  -title title
    	wrap the HTML in a page with this title
  -unsafe
    	keep raw HTML and every link: the author is trusted
Arguments:
  [file]
    	the Markdown file to read; none reads standard input
